,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T19:54:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T19:54:29Z","body":"Do we need all files from metal-cpp, or is it worth it to trim a bit what we vendor to only the files we intend to use? Since we use a monorepo approach with vendored dependencies integrated in our SCons buildsystem, we always aim to vendor only the minimal set of files that we actually need to avoid bloating the repo and Git history.\r\n\r\nmetal-cpp isn't _too_ heavy as is but it's still ~30k lines of code, so if we're using only a small subset (I didn't check), it could make sense to trim it. It's up to you to evaluate the tradeoff though, if maintaining a list of the files we want to use will significantly increase the maintenance burden, it may not be worth it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3855883483/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3855927155","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114484#issuecomment-3855927155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114484","id":3855927155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7l1Mdz","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_ur